{"id":"st422","designation":"ST 422","title":"Material Exchange Format — Mapping JPEG 2000 Codestreams into the MXF Generic Container","state":"active","suite":null,"official":{"family_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/doc/st422/","latest_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/latest/st422/","checked_at":"2026-11-11"},"scope":"JPEG 2000 is a picture-by-picture compression coding defined by ISO/IEC 15444-1 and used for both individual pictures and picture sequences. This standard specifies the mapping of JPEG 2000 codestreams conforming to ISO/IEC 15444-1 and ISO/IEC 15444-15 into a picture essence track of the MXF Generic Container in both frame-wrapped and clip-wrapped forms. SMPTE ST 422:2022 Page 4 of 23 © SMPTE 2022 – All Rights Reserved The MXF Generic Container is the native essence container of the material exchange format (MXF) file body. The MXF Generic Container is defined for the interchange of streamable audio-visual material. This standard defines the data structure at the signal interfaces of networks or storage media. This standard does not define internal storage formats for MXF compliant devices.","outline":[{"level":1,"title":"1 Scope","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"2 Conformance notation","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"3 Normative references","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"4 Terms and Definitions","page":5},{"level":1,"title":"5 JPEG 2000 mappings","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"5.1 General","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"5.2 JPEG 2000 coding summary (informative)","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"5.3 High-throughput JPEG 2000 (HTJ2K) coding summary (informative)","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"5.4 Application in the MXF Generic Container","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"5.5 \"FU\" Undefined Frame-based wrapping and \"P1\" Progressive Frame-based wrapping","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"5.6 \"I1\" interlaced Frame wrapping, 1 field per KLV Element","page":7},{"level":2,"title":"5.7 \"I2\" interlaced Frame wrapping, 2 fields per KLV Element","page":8},{"level":2,"title":"5.8 \